From 9f85b5268c570ba56a85999e6bfe8761d0d19b9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:10:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Recover update-held prompts after refused retries
 and live-writer handoff

The queue retry chain depended on drain scheduling its own successor. A transient retirement refusal or another false drain result stranded the prompt while startup recovery deferred to its still-live writer. Keep idle retries alive, sweep own queues before code-skew deferral, and release orphaned or permanently retired queue custody with marker identity fencing. Exclude queued markers from running outcomes; suppress superseded replay and warn on a queue stuck after hold lift.

Proof: new regression file failed 4 cases before the fix. 12 regression tests now pass; 148 existing focused and consumer tests pass. scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks pass.
